# Copy to backend/.env for local development. Never commit the real file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Database
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Use the POOLED host: it is the same endpoint with "-pooler" glued to the
# endpoint id, right before the first dot.
#
#   ep-cool-darkness-12345.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech          <- direct
#   ep-cool-darkness-12345-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech   <- pooled
#
# Neon's dashboard does not always offer this as a visible choice; if the string
# you copied has no "-pooler", just add it by hand and leave everything else
# untouched. The app runs as a serverless function, so pooling belongs to
# pgbouncer rather than to the process.
#
# Keep ?sslmode=require — Neon refuses plaintext connections.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@ep-xxxx-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require

# development | production — decides the Secure flag on the session cookie
# once there is a session to protect (M1).
ENVIRONMENT=development

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Access
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The only addresses that can sign in, comma separated. Everyone else gets the
# same on-screen answer and no email, so the list cannot be probed from outside.
ALLOWED_EMAILS=tu@example.com

# Where the magic link points. Locally this is the Vite dev server, in
# production the Vercel domain.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:5173

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Email (Brevo)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave BREVO_API_KEY empty in development: the login link is printed on the
# uvicorn terminal instead of being sent, which is what makes local development
# possible without a Brevo account.
#
# Two traps that each cost an afternoon:
#   - it must be the v3 API key (prefix "xkeysib-"). The SMTP key
#     ("xsmtpsib-") is for the mail relay and this endpoint rejects it.
#   - MAIL_FROM must be an address verified in Brevo under Senders. The API
#     accepts an unverified sender without complaining, and then the message
#     fails SPF/DKIM and lands in spam: it looks like it works and it does not.
BREVO_API_KEY=
MAIL_FROM=
MAIL_FROM_NAME=Wallet
